1
00:00:02,735 --> 00:00:04,735
We will make a popcorn stitch

2
00:00:05,321 --> 00:00:07,544
We are working on a double crochet row.

3
00:00:08,083 --> 00:00:11,396
Make 4 double crochets into one stitch.

4
00:00:16,344 --> 00:00:18,783
One

5
00:00:21,913 --> 00:00:23,815
Two

6
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:28,760
Three

7
00:00:31,055 --> 00:00:34,048
Four. Pull the stitch up a bit

8
00:00:34,048 --> 00:00:36,343
and take the hook off

9
00:00:36,343 --> 00:00:38,945
and go into the first one of these you just made.

10
00:00:38,945 --> 00:00:41,307
One, two, three, four.

11
00:00:41,822 --> 00:00:46,606
Insert the hook, put the stitch back,

12
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:51,052
pull, take a yarn-over

13
00:00:51,052 --> 00:00:53,508
and pull through tight.

14
00:00:53,508 --> 00:00:55,272
Here it is.

15
00:00:55,272 --> 00:00:59,142
You can also make it using 5 double crochets.

